              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 10",
              "loading": "lazy"
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-11.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 11",
              "loading": "lazy"
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-12.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 12",
              "loading": "lazy"
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-13.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 13",
              "loading": "lazy"
            }
          ],
          "columns": 3,
          "caption": "Oscar Ouyang SS26"
        },
        "E.W.USIE will be hosting appointments across the weekend, meanwhile Saul Nash will be curating a three-day pop-up. Of course, everyone will also be interested to see how Tolu Coker tops her last show, during which the king made a surprise entrance.",
        {
          "heading": "THE SEPTEMBER LOYALISTS"
        },
        {
          "gallery": [
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-14.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 14",
              "loading": "lazy"
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-15.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 15",
              "loading": "lazy"
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-16.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 16",
              "loading": "lazy"
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-17.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 17",
              "loading": "lazy"
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-18.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 18",
              "loading": "lazy"
            },
            {
              "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-19.webp",
              "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 19",
              "loading": "lazy"
            }
          ],
          "columns": 3,
          "caption": "Chopova Lowena SS26"
        },
        "Of the various fashion weeks that happen around the world and throughout the year, September’s ready-to-wear season is by far the biggest. With the rising costs of putting on a fashion show, several independent London brands prefer to show once a year, skipping the February shows in favour of September. These include brands like Ahluwalia, Chopova Lowena and Aaron Esh, meanwhile KNWLS returns to the London Fashion Week schedule following a two-year hiatus, during which it made its Milan debut.",
        {
          "heading": "THE HOT TICKETS"
        },
        {
          "image": {
            "src": "assets/images/articles/the-bag-that-everyone-claims-to-hate-and-n-20.webp",
            "alt": "Your London Fashion Week SS27 cheat sheet is here! — image 20",
            "loading": "lazy",
            "w": 1080,
            "h": 1350
          },
          "caption": "Photography Robin Galiegue"
        },
        "Historically, Burberry has been the biggest name on the LFW schedule. But this season, it’s got competition. It was announced earlier this year that McQueen would make its grand return to London after 25 years of showing in Paris. Undoubtedly, the brand will bring its supermodel casting and celebrity front row with it. Elsewhere, Christopher Kane is due to make his debut as creative director of Mulberry, which will be another major moment.",
        {
          "heading": "A MOMENT FOR THE JEWELLERY"
        },
        {
          "video": {
            "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DafsbWeCIiL/",
            "provider": "instagram"
          }
        },
        "The London jewellery scene has been slowly carving out a space for itself on the LFW schedule. Of the current NEWGEN line-up, two of the designers are exciting independent jewellers, OCTI and The Ouze. Plus, Dover Street Market will once again host its seasonal jewellery showcase, in which it celebrates emerging jewellery designers. If you thought fashion week was all about the clothes, you thought wrong!"
      ],
